{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_005","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"Computer Science > Social and Information Networks","location_hint":"paragraph 15","char_start":782,"char_end":832,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_006","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"Title: Time granularity impact on propagation of disruptions in a system-of-systems simulation of infrastructure and business networks","location_hint":"paragraph 18","char_start":897,"char_end":1031,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_007","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"Authors: Mateusz Iwo Dubaniowski , Hans Rudolf Heinimann","location_hint":"paragraph 19","char_start":1035,"char_end":1091,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_008","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"View a PDF of the paper titled Time granularity impact on propagation of disruptions in a system-of-systems simulation of infrastructure and business networks, by Mateusz Iwo Dubaniowski and 1 other authors","location_hint":"paragraph 20","char_start":1095,"char_end":1301,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_009","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"Abstract: System-of-systems (SoS) approach is often used for simulating disruptions to business and infrastructure system networks allowing for integration of several models into one simulation.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1315,"char_end":1509,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_010","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"However, the integration is frequently challenging as each system is designed individually with different characteristics, such as time granularity.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1510,"char_end":1658,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_011","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"Understanding the impact of time granularity on propagation of disruptions between businesses and infrastructure systems and finding the appropriate granularity for the SoS simulation remain as major challenges.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1659,"char_end":1870,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_012","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"To tackle these, we explore how time granularity, recovery time, and disruption size affect the propagation of disruptions between constituent systems of an SoS simulation.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":1871,"char_end":2043,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_013","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"To address this issue, we developed a High Level Architecture (HLA) simulation of 3 networks and performed a series of simulation experiments.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2044,"char_end":2186,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_014","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"Our results revealed that time granularity and especially recovery time have huge impact on propagation of disruptions.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2187,"char_end":2306,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_015","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"Consequently, we developed a model for selecting an appropriate time granularity for an SoS simulation based on expected recovery time.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2307,"char_end":2442,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_016","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"Our simulation experiments show that time granularity should be less than 1.13 of expected recovery time.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2443,"char_end":2548,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_017","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"We identified some areas for future research centered around extending the experimental factors space.","location_hint":"paragraph 22","char_start":2549,"char_end":2651,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_2fff6e91c56c_018","source_id":"src_2fff6e91c56c","source_hash":"d382603dd0dc5a1c0f5de3e122e4aa14c1704e287f3a4b936bf4ff40dbb6c1d3","text":"Comments:\n26 pages, 11 figures, 2 tables, Submitted to International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health: Special Issue on Cascading Disaster Modelling and Prevention","location_hint":"paragraph 23","char_start":2661,"char_end":2843,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-07T18:37:43.323Z"}
